1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Sgt. Kellar: Rumor has it that Division ran a black-ops group.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Sgt. Kellar: Lennox was one of them. No ties, no strings.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Interrogator: You expect me to believe we had a terror cell working for us?

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Sgt. Kellar: You can believe what you want. Fact is, Lennox was off the books, so there's no way to prove it. Very convenient.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Sgt. Kellar: Lennox did the thing in the Congo, the special in the Philippines.

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Sgt. Kellar: This was professional contract terrorism.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Sgt. Kellar: Lennox held all the cards. Started making small deviations here, little switches there…

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Sgt. Kellar: Before long, things got out of hand.

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Sgt. Kellar: Mistakes started being made. Costly, bloody mistakes.

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Sgt. Kellar: Division decided to pull the plug on him. Miami got the call.

11
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Sgt. Kellar: Lennox took them all out singlehanded. Everything changed after that.

12
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Interrogator: So what else did she tell you?

13
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Sgt. Kellar: CIA's most-wanted was Lennox. Different name, different profile, do-not-approach tag…

14
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Sgt. Kellar: …but it was him. The most-wanted terrorist was one of our own.

15
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Interrogator: And you believed her?

16
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Sgt. Kellar: Why wouldn't I?

17
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Interrogator: [What was your next operation?]

18
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Sgt. Kellar: [To destroy the steel plant used as a weapons factory.]

19
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Sgt. Kellar: [Division figured if we couldn't take out the leaders of Seventh Wave, the best thing to do was destroy their operations.]

20
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:28,000
Sgt. Kellar: [Too dangerous, too politically volatile for a regular strike.]

21
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Sgt. Kellar: [So McCarver's team was called in.]

22
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Sgt. Kellar: [There was no way anyone in their right mind would volunteer for this.]
